---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Toc from "../components/Toc.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
import { ECON } from "../consts";

const sections = [
  { href: "#lands", label: "Lands" },
  { href: "#nations", label: "Nations" },
  { href: "#vassals", label: "Vassals" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Lands & Nations · Meridian"
  description="A guide for the Lands plugin on Meridian: claiming, banks, upkeep, tiers, nations, and vassals."
  path="/lands"
  analytics
>
<main class="doc">
  <h1>Lands &amp; Nations</h1>
  <p class="lead">A guide for the Lands plugin. It covers how you claim land, how land banks and upkeep work, how lands unlock tiers, how they combine into nations, and what happens to a nation that loses a war of vassalage. For the live nation rankings, see <a href="/nations">Nations</a>.</p>

  <Toc sections={sections} />

  <h2 id="lands"><span class="num">1</span>Lands</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Run <code>/lands create &lt;name&gt;</code> to found your land free of charge. The first chunk is free.</li>
    <li>The next chunk is <strong>free</strong> too. Every chunk after that adds a fixed <strong>{ECON.chunkIncrease}</strong> to the cost of the one before it, so the larger your land gets, the more each expansion costs.</li>
    <li>When naming your land you can use a hex code to set its color on the world map, for example <code>&lt;#FF5555&gt;ExampleLand</code>. Minecraft only recognizes a specific set of hex colors.</li>
    <li>Your land has its own shared bank, separate from any individual's personal balance. Claim costs and upkeep are withdrawn from this bank, and any member can deposit into it.</li>
    <li>If the bank can't cover a cost, it falls back to the <strong>owner's</strong> personal balance.</li>
    <li>Every land pays weekly upkeep on its claimed chunks, at <strong>{ECON.landUpkeepPerChunk} per chunk</strong>.</li>
    <li>Larger lands cost more to maintain. Before you claim aggressively, make sure your land has the income to support it.</li>
    <li>You can rent or sell sub-areas of your land to other players without adding them as trusted members.</li>
    <li>Lands unlock new tiers by hitting member and wealth thresholds. The tiers are Settlement, Village, Town, Province, and Land. Each tier grants more claimable chunks and member slots, for a modest increase in upkeep.</li>
    <li>You can own only one land at a time, and be a trusted member in one additional land beyond that.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="nations"><span class="num">2</span>Nations</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Multiple lands can form a nation for <strong>{ECON.nationCreateCost}</strong>.</li>
    <li>When a land joins a nation it stops paying upkeep to the server and instead pays tax directly to the nation. The nation's leader sets that rate, up to <strong>$6,000 per chunk</strong>.</li>
    <li>In turn, the nation owes its own upkeep to the server, at <strong>{ECON.nationUpkeepPerChunk} per chunk</strong> across the combined total of its lands.</li>
    <li>Relations between nations are publicly tracked in-game.</li>
    <li>Like lands, nations can develop into higher tiers. The nation tiers are Federation, Nation, and Empire, and each one unlocks additional claiming capacity for every land in the nation.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="vassals"><span class="num">3</span>Vassals</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A nation that loses a war of vassalage is absorbed by the winning nation as restricted members.</li>
    <li>Vassals pay taxes to their overlord that can run higher than normal nation taxes.</li>
    <li>The only way to become independent again is to declare and win a war against your overlord. See <a href="/war#goals">Warfare &sect;8</a>.</li>
  </ol>

  <Callout>Warfare is the only time claimed land can be entered or captured by an enemy. Read the <a href="/war">Warfare</a> document before you get into a conflict.</Callout>
</main>
</Base>
